cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use st-report, please cite it and the works it builds on, listed under references (the methods papers of every step whose results it reports, the report's own, and the demo datasets)."
type: software
title: st-report
abstract: >-
  A Pennsieve processor, the last step of the three spatial transcriptomics workflows (Spatial
  Domain Mapping & Condition Comparison; Cell-type Deconvolution & Niches; Single-cell Spatial
  Profiling). It reads whatever upstream outputs it is given and writes one offline HTML report
  (study design, QC, spatial domains, spatially variable genes, condition comparison, cell types,
  spatial organisation, cell-cell communication, methods and citations from every step's
  provenance) and the summary tables behind it.
authors:
  - name: Pennsieve (University of Pennsylvania)
repository-code: "https://github.com/pennsieve-apps/st-report"
license: Apache-2.0
keywords:
  - spatial transcriptomics
  - report
  - Visium
  - Xenium
  - spatial domains
  - deconvolution
  - cell-cell communication
